WHAT EXACTLY IS MISSING
There are four independent reasons no evidence exists, each sufficient alone:

1. The system has never traded real money.
engine/cmd/antigravity/main.go:449 hardcodes execution.NewPaperClient(initialPaperBalanceUSD). No live broker execution path exists for the BTC futures scalper. The system is a simulator.

2. Paper trade records are not persisted across restarts.
PaperClosedTrade lives in a Go slice in the PaperOMS struct. Render restarts wipe it. The MongoDB sync runs client-side (browser-triggered) and is not called from the engine directly. The $20–$0.56 PnL figures in the forensics report were accumulated during a single engine session that did not survive to disk.

3. The signal pipeline kills 98–99.5% of signals before execution.
The 7-layer funnel — 30-strategy cap, maxApprovedSignals=2, confidence floor 0.82, minSelectiveScore 1.30, bridge parking, daily loss $83 floor — produces approximately 2 executed trades per day from 605 strategies. At that rate, reaching 100 trades per strategy would take years per strategy.

4. No backtest has ever been run to completion and saved.
engine/cmd/backtest/main.go exists. No output files from it exist anywhere. engine/internal/backtest/v2/ and v3/ have complete, correct metric calculation code. They have never been executed against historical data with results saved to disk.

